  "live_records": {
    "q-131973": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131973",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{3}t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3}⟩$ for $t\\ge 0,$ use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(0,0,0).$",
      "worked_solution": "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(0,0,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨0,0,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨\\sqrt{3}t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3}⟩ & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}t=0 \\\\ {t}^{2}=0 \\\\ {t}^{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=0.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(0,0,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{3}t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,2t,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,2(0),\\,3({0}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3},0,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3+0+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
