    "q-64755": {
      "dom_id": "step-q64755",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Find the curvature of the curve $r(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩$, as a function of $t.$",
      "worked_solution": "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩=⟨8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}}=\\sqrt{100{cos}^{2}⁡2t}=10|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t),-6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩=⟨-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,0⟩\\times ⟨-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & 0 \\\\ -16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ -16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =(96\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-96\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{0}{(10|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t|)^{3}}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
